<title>USA: NBA BASKETBALL-CAREER COACHING RECORD OF RICK PITINO.</title>
<headline>NBA BASKETBALL-CAREER COACHING RECORD OF RICK PITINO.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Career coaching record of Rick</p>
<p>Pitino, who left the University of Kentucky on Tuesday to</p>
<p>become head coach of the Boston Celtics (tabulate under year,</p>
<p>team, wins, losses, winning percentage):</p>
<p>Professional</p>
<p>Regular Season</p>
<p> 1987-88 New York	     38    44   .463</p>
<p> 1988-89 New York	     52    30   .634</p>
<p>    Totals			90    74   .549</p>
<p>Playoffs</p>
<p> 1987-88 New York		1     3   .250</p>
<p> 1988-89 New York		5     4   .556</p>
<p>     Totals			6     7   .462</p>
<p>College</p>
<p> 1978-79 Boston University  17     9   .654</p>
<p> 1979-80 Boston University  21     9   .700</p>
<p> 1980-81 Boston University  13    14   .481</p>
<p> 1981-82 Boston University  19     9   .678</p>
<p> 1982-83 Boston University  21    10   .677</p>
<p> 1985-86 Providence	   17    14   .548</p>
<p> 1986-87 Providence	   25     9   .735 *</p>
<p> 1989-90 Kentucky	     14    14   .500</p>
<p> 1990-91 Kentucky	     22     6   .786</p>
<p> 1991-92 Kentucky	     29     7   .805</p>
<p> 1992-93 Kentucky	     30     4   .882 **</p>
<p> 1993-94 Kentucky	     27     7   .794</p>
<p> 1994-95 Kentucky	     28     5   .848</p>
<p> 1995-96 Kentucky	     34     2   .944 ***</p>
<p> 1996-97 Kentucky	     35     5   .875 ****</p>
<p>    TOTALS		     352   124   .739</p>
<p>    *    - lost to Syracuse in Final Four</p>
<p>    **   - lost to Michigan in Final Four</p>
<p>***  - beat Syracuse for National Championship</p>
<p>**** - Lost to Arizona in NCAA Championship Game</p>
